<%# locals: (label:, figure:, tail:, percentage:, variant:, aria_label:, lead: false, hatched: false) %>
<%# One bar with its label and figure above it. lead: the on-duty fact, a size up and in heading weight
    with only the goal stepping back, and the percentage printed in the bar; hatched: the sign-ups
    estimate, striped (progress-projected) so it reads as "not yet" at any contrast.
    Both bars are the :lg height so the pair lines up and the figure can be read in dust or glare.
    The percentage prints only where it fits inside the fill: a two-digit label and its end padding
    take about 32px, 13% of the bar on a 320px phone. Below that the figure above says it. A full bar
    says it without a number, and white on the green fill fails contrast in dark mode. %>
<div class="grid gap-1 text-stone-subtle">
  <div class="flex flex-wrap items-baseline justify-between gap-x-4 gap-y-1 text-base tabular-nums <%= "font-semibold text-heading" if lead %>">
    <span><%= label %></span>
    <span><%= tag.span figure, class: ("text-lg" if lead) %> <%= tag.span tail, class: ("font-normal text-stone-subtle" if lead) %></span>
  </div>
  <%= ui_progress_bar percentage, variant,
                      size: :lg,
                      label: (true if lead && percentage.between?(13, 99)),
                      bar_class: ("progress-projected" if hatched),
                      class: "ring-1 ring-inset ring-base-content/35",
                      aria: { label: aria_label } %>
</div>
